From: leerep <leerep@163.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tools/quilt: fix the -j build race on po/quilt.pot

quilt 0.69 builds the po/quilt.pot prerequisite list with
$(wildcard */*.in), evaluated when make reads the Makefile.  The list
therefore contains compat/column.in only while that file still exists, but
configure deletes compat/column.in as soon as it finds a column(1) on the
host and replaces it with a symlink.  When the two steps overlap the
prerequisite is recorded and then disappears:

  make[4]: *** No rule to make target 'compat/column.in', needed by 'po/quilt.pot'.  Stop.

A serialised build never hits it because the delete and the read cannot
overlap; under -j$(nproc) the quilt host tool fails and the build stops
before the target tree is even started.

Recreate the file right before the build so the prerequisite always
resolves, and build quilt serially: it is a small host tool that gains
nothing from parallel compilation.

Signed-off-by: leerep <leerep@163.com>
---
 tools/quilt/Makefile | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/quilt/Makefile b/tools/quilt/Makefile
index 8fe69ca1e8..da588daaf8 100644
--- a/tools/quilt/Makefile
+++ b/tools/quilt/Makefile
@@ -22,7 +22,16 @@ define Host/Configure
 endef
 
 define Host/Compile
-	$(MAKE) -C $(HOST_BUILD_DIR) SHELL="$(BASH)" all
+	# quilt 0.69 computes the po/quilt.pot prerequisites with $(wildcard */*.in)
+	# when make reads this Makefile, so compat/column.in is listed while it still
+	# exists; configure removes it as soon as the host has column(1) and replaces
+	# it with a symlink.  Under -j the delete can land between the read and the
+	# rule, leaving a prerequisite that can never be built:
+	#   No rule to make target 'compat/column.in', needed by 'po/quilt.pot'
+	# Recreate the file so the prerequisite always resolves, and build quilt
+	# serially: it is a small host tool that gains nothing from parallelism.
+	mkdir -p $(HOST_BUILD_DIR)/compat && touch $(HOST_BUILD_DIR)/compat/column.in
+	$(MAKE) -j1 -C $(HOST_BUILD_DIR) SHELL="$(BASH)" all
 endef
 
 define Host/Install

-- 
2.43.0
